<% content_for :title, "Choices (radio & checkbox groups)" %>
<%
  roles = DocsController.roles
  plans = [["Starter", "starter"], ["Growth", "growth"], ["Enterprise", "enterprise"]]
  # One icon per plan, so the card variant's icon slot shows what it is for: a person for one
  # seat, people for a team, a rising line for scale.
  plan_icon_paths = {
    "starter" => [tag.path(d: "M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"), tag.circle(cx: 12, cy: 7, r: 4)],
    "growth"  => [tag.path(d: "M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"), tag.circle(cx: 9, cy: 7, r: 4),
                  tag.path(d: "M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"), tag.path(d: "M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75")],
    "scale"   => [tag.path(d: "M23 6l-9.5 9.5-5-5L1 18"), tag.path(d: "M17 6h6v6")]
  }
  plan_icon = ->(plan) { tag.svg(safe_join(plan_icon_paths.fetch(plan.id)), class: "size-5", viewBox: "0 0 24 24",
                                 fill: "none", stroke: "currentColor", "stroke-width": 2,
                                 "stroke-linecap": "round", "stroke-linejoin": "round") }
  card_plans = [Struct.new(:id, :name, :tagline).new("starter", "Starter", "One project, one seat."),
                Struct.new(:id, :name, :tagline).new("growth", "Growth", "Ten projects, unlimited seats."),
                Struct.new(:id, :name, :tagline).new("scale", "Scale", "Everything, plus priority support.")]
%>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Forms</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Choices <span class="text-muted-foreground font-semibold">(radio &amp; checkbox groups)</span></h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A radio group (<code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">multiple: false</code>)
    or a checkbox group (<code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">multiple: true</code>)
    over real inputs, with the names, ids and hidden field
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">collection_radio_buttons</code> and
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">collection_check_boxes</code> render.
    Unchecking every box clears the association instead of silently keeping the old value. Arrow keys, Space,
    single selection and reset are the browser's own — the kit adds JavaScript for one thing only, below.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="choices-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background grid gap-8 p-12 mb-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
  <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[plan]") do |field| %>
    <% field.with_label { "Plan" } %>
    <% field.with_control(Ui::ChoicesComponent, options: plans, checked: "growth",
                          disabled_values: ["enterprise"]) %>
    <% field.with_description { "One choice. Enterprise is on request." } %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[role_ids]") do |field| %>
    <% field.with_label { "Roles" } %>
    <% field.with_control(Ui::ChoicesComponent, multiple: true, collection: roles, value_method: :id,
                          text_method: :name, description_method: :tagline, checked: [1]) %>
    <% field.with_description { "Several choices, each with its own description line." } %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Card variant %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">The card variant</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">variant: :card</code> makes the
  whole card the target — text, description, icon and padding all check the input, and focus still lands on the input
  itself. Columns are your <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">class:</code>,
  so cards stack at phone widths unless you say otherwise.
</p>
<div id="choices-card-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-12 mb-8">
  <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "card[plan]") do |field| %>
    <% field.with_label { "Billing plan" } %>
    <% field.with_control(Ui::ChoicesComponent, variant: :card, collection: card_plans, value_method: :id,
                          text_method: :name, description_method: :tagline, icon_method: plan_icon,
                          checked: "growth", class: "sm:grid-cols-3") %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Required %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Required</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  A required radio group is native: every radio gets <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">required</code>,
  and the browser blocks the submission. A required checkbox group has no native equivalent —
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">required</code> on a checkbox
  means <em>that</em> box — so the kit's one controller, <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">ui--choices</code>,
  makes it mean "at least one", and a visually hidden hint tells a screen reader user what the
  <span aria-hidden="true">*</span> means. With JavaScript off, the server's validation is what catches it.
</p>
<div id="choices-required-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-12 mb-8">
  <form id="choices-required-form" class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "required[plan]", required: true) do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Plan" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::ChoicesComponent, options: plans) %>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "required[role_ids]", required: true) do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Roles" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::ChoicesComponent, multiple: true, collection: roles, value_method: :id,
                            text_method: :name) %>
    <% end %>
    <div class="sm:col-span-2">
      <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(type: "submit", id: "choices-required-submit")) { "Try to submit" } %>
    </div>
  </form>
</div>

<%# Locked values %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Locked values</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">disabled_values:</code> renders a
  choice the user can't change. A disabled input never submits, so Rails' own markup deletes a locked value on every
  save; the kit carries a checked locked value in a hidden input instead, and the save keeps what the form showed.
</p>
<p class="text-sm mb-3 rounded-md border border-border bg-muted/50 p-4">
  <strong>A locked checkbox is not authorization.</strong> A hidden input can be removed or edited in the browser, and a
  disabled one re-enabled. The server still decides what a user may change: filter or merge locked values there.
</p>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  This group is required too, and a locked checked value counts: the group is satisfied because that value is
  carried, so the browser doesn't block a submission the server would have accepted.
</p>
<div id="choices-locked-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-12 mb-8">
  <form id="choices-locked-form">
  <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "locked[role_ids]", required: true) do |field| %>
    <% field.with_label { "Roles" } %>
    <% field.with_control(Ui::ChoicesComponent, multiple: true, collection: roles, value_method: :id,
                          text_method: :name, checked: [1, 2], disabled_values: [1]) %>
    <% field.with_description { "Admin is checked and locked — it posts through a hidden input beside the group." } %>
  <% end %>
  </form>
</div>

<%# Round trip %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">A server round trip</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  A real form, posted to a real action. Clear both groups and save: the checkbox group still posts
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">role_ids[]=""</code> — the entry that
  empties an association — and the 422 comes back with the model's errors on both Fields and the submitted choices checked.
</p>
<div id="choices-round-trip-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-12 mb-8">
  <%= render "docs/choices_round_trip", membership: DemoMembership.new(role_ids: [1], plan: "starter"), roles: DocsController.roles, submission: 0 %>
</div>

<%# include_hidden %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">include_hidden: false</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  Rails' option, with Rails' default of <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">true</code>.
  Turn it off and a group with nothing checked posts no key at all: <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">role_ids=</code>
  is never called, the old association survives, and a form whose only field is this one raises
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">ParameterMissing</code>. Pass it only
  when "no key means no change" is what you want.
</p>

<%# Sizes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Sizes</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">size:</code> moves the card, not the list. A card is a
  control, so each one is at least the step's own control height and a one-line card lines up with the Input or Select
  beside it. A list row isn't a control of its own: it takes a flat 24px floor (WCAG 2.5.8) at every step, so the
  three lists below are the same height. Content makes a choice taller; a step never makes it shorter.
</p>
<div id="choices-sizes-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-start gap-8 p-12 mb-8">
  <% %i[sm default lg].each do |step| %>
    <div class="grid gap-4">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><%= step %></p>
      <%= render Ui::ChoicesComponent.new(name: "size_#{step}[plan]", options: plans, size: step, checked: "growth",
                                          aria: { label: "Plan (#{step})" }) %>
      <%= render Ui::ChoicesComponent.new(name: "card_size_#{step}[plan]", options: plans, size: step, variant: :card,
                                          checked: "growth", aria: { label: "Plan card (#{step})" }) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#choices-usage" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="choices-usage" class="text-card-foreground"><%= h(example_choices_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["name",                "String",        "required", "The control's HTML name, e.g. \"user[role_ids]\". With multiple: true, [] is appended unless it's already there."],
        ["multiple",            "Boolean",       "false",    "false renders radios, true renders checkboxes — the same keyword select(multiple: true) uses for the same submission change."],
        ["collection",          "Enumerable",    "nil",      "With value_method: and text_method:, exactly as collection_check_boxes takes them. Each accepts a symbol or a proc."],
        ["options",             "Array or Hash", "nil",      "What options_for_select takes: [\"S\", \"M\"], [[\"Draft\", \"draft\"]] or { \"Draft\" => \"draft\" }. Grouped shapes raise — a radiogroup can't own groups."],
        ["model / enum",        "Class, Symbol", "nil",      "A model and one of its enums. Labels come from human_attribute_name; the submitted value is the enum key."],
        ["checked",             "Object/Array",  "nil",      "Rails' own checked: — the value or values that start checked, compared as strings. Inside a model-bound Field it comes from the record."],
        ["disabled_values",     "Array",         "nil",      "Values rendered disabled. A checked one is carried by a hidden input, so saving doesn't delete it."],
        ["include_hidden",      "Boolean",       "true",     "Rails' option with Rails' default: the blank entry that lets unchecking everything clear the attribute."],
        ["required",            "Boolean",       "false",    "Radios: required on every radio. Checkboxes: the marker, the screen-reader hint and ui--choices' \"at least one\"."],
        ["disabled",            "Boolean",       "false",    "Renders <fieldset disabled>, so every input and hidden field is disabled and the attribute is left untouched."],
        ["form",                "String",        "nil",      "The id of a form elsewhere on the page; goes on every input and the hidden fields, as in Rails."],
        ["variant",             "Symbol",        ":list",    "One of :list, :card. A card is a bordered box with the indicator, an optional icon, and the text column."],
        ["size",                "Symbol",        ":default", "One of :sm, :default, :lg — a card's minimum height, from the same tokens Input and Select read. No visible effect on the list variant, whose rows take a flat 24px floor."],
        ["description_method",  "Symbol/Proc",   "nil",      "A second line per choice. Needs collection:, since there is no object to call it on otherwise."],
        ["icon_method",         "Symbol/Proc",   "nil",      "Decorative HTML-safe markup per choice, aria-hidden. Needs collection: too."],
        ["required_message",    "String",        "nil",      "Overrides rails_ui_kit.choices.required_message for this instance."],
        ["class",               "String",        "nil",      "Merged onto the fieldset — the caller always wins. This is where grid columns go."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Accessibility %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>The group is a <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;fieldset&gt;</code>:
      <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">role="radiogroup"</code> for radios,
      a plain group for checkboxes. Inside a Field it's named by the field's label, which renders without
      <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">for</code> — pointing that at the
      first input would make clicking "Roles" toggle Admin. Outside a Field, name it yourself with
      <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria: { label: }</code>.</li>
  <li>Each input is named by its own text and described by its own description line, so a wrapping label never reads
      as "Pro Unlimited projects". The icon is <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-hidden</code>.</li>
  <li>Focus is always on a real input — no card, label or fieldset is focusable, and nothing adds a
      <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">tabindex</code>. In the card
      variant the ring is drawn on the card, and only for the keyboard.</li>
  <li>A checkbox never carries <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">required</code>
      or <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-required</code>: both would
      say every box is required. The group says it once, in the hint.</li>
  <li>A choice holds no interactive content. A link inside a card isn't supported — it would be a target inside a target.</li>
</ul>

<%# Not this %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  A collection too long to show as a list is a <%= link_to "Select", select_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>, not a
  group of inputs. A searchable "pick several" is a multi-select combobox, which is Select's territory and isn't built yet.
  An on/off setting that takes effect immediately is a switch, which the kit doesn't ship.
</p>
